- How would you handle varying campaign setup costs or penalties per segment length?

## Why This Is Asked
This problem extends the classic Longest Palindromic Subsequence (LPS) problem by allowing up to k character deletions, requiring a 3D DP formulation. It tests understanding of subsequence DP with additional constraints, careful boundary handling, and the ability to reconstruct the solution path.

## Key Concepts
- Longest Palindromic Subsequence with deletions
- 3D DP (i, j, d) where d represents remaining deletions
- Path reconstruction for deletion decisions
- Time/space complexity: O(n²·k) time, O(n²·k) space

## Code Example
```javascript
function longestPalindromicSubseqWithDeletions(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n }, () =>
    Array.from({ length: n }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(0))
  );

  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    for (let d = 0; d <= k; d++) {
      dp[i][i][d] = 1;
    }
  }

  for (let len = 2; len <= n; len++) {
    for (let i = 0; i + len <= n; i++) {
      const j = i + len - 1;
      for (let d = 0; d <= k; d++) {
        if (s[i] === s[j]) {
          dp[i][j][d] = Math.max(dp[i][j][d], (len > 2 ? dp[i + 1][j - 1][d] : 0) + 2);
        }
        if (d > 0) {
          dp[i][j][d] = Math.max(dp[i][j][d], dp[i + 1][j][d - 1], dp[i][j - 1][d - 1]);
        }
      }
    }
  }

  return dp[0][n - 1][k];
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design DP over partitions with a non-linear segment value, including reconstruction of segments. Encourages using prefix sums for fast segment sums and careful indexing to enforce exactly k non-empty contiguous blocks. Also invites discussion of time/space trade-offs and potential optimizations.

## Key Concepts

- Prefix sums for quick segment sums
- DP over partitions with exact k blocks
- Reconstructing the chosen boundaries via a prev table

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxPartition(A, k, c){
  const n = A.length;
  const P = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++) P[i] = P[i-1] + A[i-1];
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1},()=>new Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const prev = Array.from({length:n+1},()=>new Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++) dp[i][1] = (P[i]-P[0])**2 - c, prev[i][1] = 0;
  for(let t=2;t<=k;t++){
    for(let i=t;i<=n;i++){
      for(let j=t-1;j<=i-1;j++){
        const val = dp[j][t-1] + (P[i]-P[j])**2 - c;
        if(val > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t] = val; prev[i][t] = j; }
      }
    }
  }
  // recover endpoints via backtracking
  return {best: dp[n][k], prev};
}
``` 

