## Why This Is Asked
Tests a novel fixed-gap non-crossing pairing constraint, a natural extension of classic non-crossing matching problems, while probing DP state design and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- DP over prefixes with fixed pair distance
- Non-crossing/disjoint constraint handling
- Backpointers for reconstruction
- Space/time optimization trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxFixedGapPairs(A, d, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-Infinity));
  const take = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(false));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
      dp[i][t] = dp[i - 1][t];
      if (t > 0 && i - d - 1 >= 0) {
        const cand = dp[i - d - 1][t - 1] + A[i - 1] * A[i - d - 1];
        if (cand > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = cand;
          take[i][t] = true;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  const pairs = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0 && i > 0) {
    if (take[i][t]) {
      pairs.push([i - d, i]); // 1-based indices of the pair
      i = i - d - 1;
      t--;
    } else {
      i--;
    }
  }
  pairs.reverse();
  return { value: dp[n][k], pairs };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This gauges ability to cast a line-wrapping task into a clear 1D DP with a non-linear line cost and a reconstruction path. It tests handling of last-line quirks and feasibility checks.

## Key Concepts
- 1D DP over word indices; dp[n] = 0 as base.
- Prefix sums to compute line width in O(1) per extension.
- Cost function uses squared unused space; last line excluded.
- Reconstruct solution via next indices.
- Time: O(n^2); Space: O(n).

## Code Example
```javascript
function minWrap(words, W) {
  const n = words.length;
  const pref = new Array(n + 1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) pref[i + 1] = pref[i] + words[i];
  const dp = new Array(n + 1).fill(Infinity);
  const nxt = new Array(n).fill(-1);
  dp[n] = 0;
  for (let i = n - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
    for (let j = i; j < n; j++) {
      const width = (pref[j + 1] - pref[i]) + (j - i);
      if (width <= W) {
        const cost = (W - width) * (W - width) + dp[j + 1];
        if (cost < dp[i]) { dp[i] = cost; nxt[i] = j + 1; }
      } else break;
    }
  }
  // reconstruction omitted for brevity
  return { minPenalty: dp[0], next: nxt };
}
```

